   MMoouunntt pprrooppaaggaattiioonn
       The   bind‐mount   mount   objects   created   by   ooppeenn__ttrreeee()    with
       OOPPEENN__TTRREEEE__CCLLOONNEE  are  not  associated  with  the mount namespace of the
       calling process.  Instead, each mount object is placed in a newly allo‐
       cated "anonymous" mount namespace associated with the calling process.

       One of the side‐effects of this is  that  (unlike  bind‐mounts  created
       with mmoouunntt(2)), mount propagation (as described in mmoouunntt__nnaammeessppaacceess(7))
       will  not  be  applied  to bind‐mounts created by ooppeenn__ttrreeee() until the
       bind‐mount is attached with mmoovvee__mmoouunntt(2), at which point the mount ob‐
       ject will be associated with the mount namespace where it was  attached
       and  mount  propagation  will  resume.  Note that any mount propagation
       events that occurred before the mount object was attached will  _n_o_t  be
       propagated to the mount object, even after it is attached.

